    "answer": {
      "short": "a and e; b and d; c and f.\n\nEach pair has equal gradients.",
      "worked": "For a:\n$$\\begin{align*}4y&=-x+8\\\\y&=-\\frac14x+2\\end{align*}$$\nFor b:\n$$y=3x+6.$$\nFor d:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac13y&=x-2\\\\y&=3x-6\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradients are $m_a=-\\frac14$, $m_b=3$, $m_c=-3$, $m_d=3$, $m_e=-\\frac14$ and $m_f=-3$.\n\nLines with equal gradients are parallel, so the pairs are a and e, b and d, and c and f.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
